ent.py:212-229). That is its documented posture and it is unchanged.\n- Input-side behavior inside the moved code is unchanged:\n  - _enforce_prompt_defense blocks on bad input and allows on internal errors;\n  - _validate_skill_reference blocks when any sub-check fails (ADR-051).\n\n5. Effect on adopters\n- A fresh install copies every top-level _lib entry except tests, test_isolation.py and testing.py (scripts/install.sh:1520-1550; exclusion rule at scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107). So _lib/agent_spawn/ ships.\n- An upgrade treats .claude/hooks as one whole target.\n- These two files change no environment default, model, effort setting or block condition.\n- A hand-patched check_agent_spawn.py now has to be re-patched in these modules. Condition 7 declares this.\n\n6. Writes\n- Neither module writes files.\n- The only side effect is _audit_emit.emit_generic in _emit_prompt_defense_event. It is guarded and fails open, as before.\n\n7. Declared conditions\n- Condition 5 is true for this package: \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\" is in _KERNEL_PATHS at check_arbitration_kernel.py:310.\n- Condition 7 matches what this payload shows.\n- Nothing in these two files makes any declared condition false.\n\nFINDINGS\nNo P0. No P1.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n\nP2-1. The secret scan on SKILL.md files only looks at the first ~117 characters (pre-existing).\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/skill_reference.py:250-251 and prompt_rules.py:112-128.\n- Cause: _skill_ref_validate_hash_and_redact calls _redact.redact_secrets(text) with the default max_chars=120 (_lib/redact.py:117, 120, 186-194). The output is collapsed to one line and cut to 117 characters plus \"...\". The token check at :251 therefore only sees the first ~117 characters of SKILL.md, which is the frontmatter.\n- Two more gaps:\n  - redact_secrets truncates its input at 64 KiB (redact.py:108, 144-146), while reference files may be up to 1 MiB;\n  - the [AWS_SECRET] token emitted by redact.py:102 is missing from _SECRET_TOKENS_IN_OUTPUT.\n- Failure scenario: a SKILL.md with a credential anywhere in its body passes sub-check 11, and a reference-mode sub-agent loads it into its context. ADR-051 sub-check 11 and docs/threat-model.md:1884 present this check as the mitigation for \"Secret leak embedded in SKILL.md\". The existing test (tests/test_check_agent_spawn_skill_reference.py:229-263) puts the key right after a ~50-character frontmatter, inside the window, so it cannot catch this.\n- Not a regression of this delta: the code is identical in the old single file.\n- Rated P2, not P1: the file is already committed and protected as a canonical file, and the default inline SKILL CONTENT path has no scan at all. Raise it to P1 if the Owner treats threat-model row 10 as load-bearing.\n- Minimal fix:\n  - call redact_secrets(text, max_chars=0) over 64 KiB chunks, or use a scan API that does not truncate;\n  - add \"[AWS_SECRET]\" to the token set;\n  - add tests with the key placed after character 200 and after 64 KiB.\n\nP2-2. Comments describe the spawn-prompt secret scan wrongly (pre-existing text, shipped again unchanged).\n- Where: prompt_rules.py:163-170 and 213-214.\n- What they say: the scan rejects by default, CEO_SPAWN_SECRET_SCAN=0 turns it off, and a bypass is logged as veto_triggered(reason_code=spawn_secret_scan_bypassed).\n- What the code does: line 221 runs the scan only when the variable is exactly \"1\", so it is off by default. No spawn_secret_scan_bypassed event is emitted anywhere under .claude/hooks.\n- Fix: say \"opt-in via CEO_SPAWN_SECRET_SCAN=1; no bypass event\".\n\nP2-3. Comments orphaned by the split (cosmetic).\n- prompt_rules.py:364 says _OVERLAP_LOOKBACK_S is re-exported \"below\"; it actually comes from file_assignment.py:7 through the wiring at the end of the hook file.\n- prompt_rules.py:397-404 describes a marker hash whose code is at file_assignment.py:496.\n- check_agent_spawn.py:225-227 keeps the \"[END]\" banner of the prompt-defense block, whose \"[BEGIN]\" banner is now in prompt_rules.py.\n- Fix: move or remove these comments.\n\nP2-4. The two modules cannot be used on their own.\n- Their functions find os, re, Path, hashlib, unicodedata, _redact and the advisories regexes only through the hook module's globals.\n- So a direct \"from _lib.agent_spawn.skill_reference import _validate_skill_reference\" fails with NameError when the function is called.\n- No caller in the tree does this today; the only importer is check_agent_spawn.py:643.\n- skill_reference.py has a docstring that says so; prompt_rules.py has none.\n- Fix: add the same docstring to prompt_rules.py, or a test that fails on direct use.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Both new modules match the pre-split hook code text for text, are wired back into the hook's namespace without a missing name, a name collision or an inverted fail direction, ship to adopters by both install and upgrade, and leave conditions 5 and 7 true; the only issues found are pre-existing or cosmetic P2s."},"ttft_ms":8777,"type":"result","duration_ms":434730,"uuid":"c014861a-c0b4-4905-bdd0-6a7bb5eb7eae","ttft_stream_ms":2104,"time_to_request_ms":33,"first_content_frame_ms":2105,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":72,"outputTokens":40138,"cacheReadInputTokens":3147085,"cacheCreationInputTokens":135911,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.519753,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":28014,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":135911,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-20T15:54:23.997Z"}
